  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
I'm sorry to hear you're suffering from severe insomnia — that's truly exhausting, both physically and mentally 🙏

Here's what Master Lu recommends for daily recitation:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 7 times daily
Before reciting, pray: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health and strength."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 7 times daily
Before reciting, pray: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom, a calm and clear mind, and remove my worries."*
⚠️ Do not recite after 10pm, or during thunderstorms/heavy rain.

📿 **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** — 1 to 3 times daily (start with 1)
Before reciting, pray: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], help me repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."*
⚠️ Do not recite after 10pm.

---

For insomnia specifically, the **Heart Sutra** is especially helpful — Master Lu teaches that it opens wisdom and removes mental disturbances. If your mind tends to race at night, reciting the Heart Sutra during the day can help calm and clear it over time.

If you haven't recited before, start simple — just the **Great Compassion Mantra 3 times + Heart Sutra 3 times** each day. Consistency matters more than volume.

🔗 Follow-along recitation videos: https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Keep reciting sincerely. Guan Yin Bodhisattva will bless you 🙏

