It's tough when there's constant conflict at home 🙏

Master Lu's teaching is clear on this — interpersonal conflicts, including family friction, often have roots in karmic ties from previous lives. The good news is that recitation can genuinely help dissolve these knots.

Here's a simple starting point:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒)** — 3 recitations per day
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], and grant me good health and inner strength."*

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经)** — 3 recitations per day
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom and help me remove frustration and agitation."*
⚠️ Please do not recite after 10pm.

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots (解结咒)** — 21 recitations per day
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [family member's name] resolve our karmic knots."*

The Heart Sutra is especially powerful here — Master Lu taught that it opens wisdom and helps reduce conflict. You can also recite it *for* your family members silently (they don't need to know), saying their name in the prayer.

To learn the recitations, follow along with this teaching video:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

---

