═══ CHIP4-en My child is rebell — guard: stripped ═══
Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
It's really hard when your child seems to push against everything you do. That tension — wanting to connect but feeling like you're hitting a wall — is exhausting and painful. 🙏

The good news is that Master Lu's teachings give us both a practical path and a way to understand what's happening beneath the surface.

**Understanding the situation**

Master Lu teaches that when children are in conflict with their parents, it is often connected to karmic ties from previous lives — the child may have come to collect karmic debts, or there may be unresolved karmic knots between you. This doesn't mean you've done something wrong. It simply means there's spiritual work to do alongside the parenting.

**For your own emotions first**

Before you can help your child, you need to stabilise yourself. A calm parent creates a calmer environment. Each day, try:

📿 **《Heart Sutra》** — recite for yourself to open wisdom and reduce frustration
Pray: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me [your full name], help me to gain wisdom, keep my mind clear and calm, and remove my worries."*
⚠️ Do not recite after 10pm

📿 **《Great Compassion Mantra》** 3–7 times daily — to strengthen your energy and keep you grounded
Pray: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me [your full name] to be healthy and strong."*

**For your child**

So the recommended recitations for your child are:

📿 **《Heart Sutra》** — recite on your child's behalf, as many times as you can
Pray: *"May Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless [child's full name] to gain wisdom and be cooperative."*

📿 **《Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots (解结咒)》** — 21 times daily
Pray: *"May Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me [your full name] and [child's full name] to resolve our karmic conflicts."*

📿 **《Great Compassion Mantra》** — for a physically healthy child, 3–7 times daily is appropriate
*(Note: Master Lu advises not to recite excessive amounts of the Great Compassion Mantra for rebellious children, as it may increase their spiritual strength and make them harder to discipline — 7 times is a good limit)*

**One more thing**

Master Lu also reminds us: don't use an adult's way of thinking to restrain the innocent and playful nature of children. Sometimes what looks like rebellion is just the energy of youth. Patience, compassion, and consistent recitation will gradually soften the relationship.

Recite steadily. Bodhisattva will help the karmic knots between you slowly dissolve. 🙏

*Reference: Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3 (Q114, Q127); Buddhism Q&A (Q127)*

═══ CHIP5-en I am new to 心灵法门,  — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: I am new to 心灵法门, what is the first step?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Welcome 🙏 You've come to a beautiful place to start.

The Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door, taught by Master Lu Jun Hong, is a practice centred on **Guan Yin Bodhisattva**. The core is simple: chant sutras daily, make vows, perform life liberation, repent, and study Master Lu's wisdom teachings.

---

## Your First Step: Start Chanting These Two

For a complete beginner, Master Lu recommends starting with just **two sutras**:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** (Ta Pei Chou) — **3–7 times daily**
Before chanting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health and safety."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** (Hsin Ching) — **3–7 times daily**
Before chanting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom."*

⚠️ Do not chant the Heart Sutra after 10PM, or during thunderstorms/heavy rain.

---

## How to Learn the Chanting

You don't need to know Chinese characters — just follow along with the video:

🔗 **Teaching videos:** https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

---

## The Third Pillar (add this once you're comfortable)

Once the above two feel natural, you'll add:

📿 **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** (Li Fo Ta Chan Hui Wen) — start with **1 time daily**
This helps repent and clear karmic obstacles. Start at just 1 recitation — don't rush to increase.

---

## The Five Pillars of This Practice

Master Lu taught **five core methods**:
1. **Chanting sutras** (daily practice)
2. **Making vows** (sincere commitments to Bodhisattva)
3. **Life liberation** (releasing animals mercifully)
4. **Great Repentance**
5. **Studying Master Lu's wisdom** (Bai Hua Fo Fa — Plain Words on Buddhism)

There are also smaller mantras for specific situations — for example, the Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots for relationship difficulties, or the Cundi Dharani for wishes — but those come naturally as you progress. No need to rush 🙏

---

Consistency matters far more than quantity. Even 3 recitations done sincerely every day is a beautiful start.

Have you had any chance to look at Master Lu's teachings before, or is this completely new to you? 🙏

